From be7cc3a61fe4d84e725738ecfe4224b75b99f819 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:13:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Verify source signatures with openpgpverify

Replace the GnuPG-based %gpgverify with %openpgpverify, which uses
Sequoia sqv and takes the same options, as part of the Fedora 45 Change
https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Sequoia_openpgpverify

Release bumped with a changelog entry.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 slurp.spec | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/slurp.spec b/slurp.spec
index 1a1206e..8356bc0 100644
--- a/slurp.spec
+++ b/slurp.spec
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 Name:		slurp
 Version:	1.5.0
-Release:	7%{?dist}
+Release:	8%{?dist}
 Summary:	Select a region in Sway
 
 License:	MIT
@@ -17,14 +17,14 @@ BuildRequires:	pkgconfig(xkbcommon)
 BuildRequires:	scdoc
 BuildRequires:	meson
 BuildRequires:	gcc
-BuildRequires:	gnupg2
+BuildRequires:	openpgpverify
 
 %description
 Slurp is a command-line tool that allows the user to visually select a region
 and prints it to the standard output.
 
 %prep
-%{gpgverify} --keyring='%{SOURCE2}' --signature='%{SOURCE1}' --data='%{SOURCE0}'
+%{openpgpverify} --keyring='%{SOURCE2}' --signature='%{SOURCE1}' --data='%{SOURCE0}'
 %autosetup
 
 %build
@@ -40,6 +40,9 @@ and prints it to the standard output.
 %{_mandir}/man1/slurp.1*
 
 %changelog
+* Thu Oct 22 2026 Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com> - 1.5.0-8
+- Verify upstream source signatures with openpgpverify
+
 * Fri Jul 17 2026 Fedora Release Engineering <releng@fedoraproject.org> - 1.5.0-7
 - Rebuilt for https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Fedora_45_Mass_Rebuild
 
-- 
